<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Subscribe — {{ brand.PUBLICATION }}</title>
<meta name="description" content="Get {{ brand.PUBLICATION }} in your inbox, {{ brand.CADENCE }}.">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ brand.SITE_URL }}/subscribe.html">
{#- The redirect that makes the public URL ours.

    The signup form has to live on the mailing-list provider — a static site
    cannot accept a form POST, which is the whole reason this project pays
    anyone at all. But the URL that gets printed, posted to a forum and pasted
    into a club's chat should be theloneaquarist.com/subscribe, permanently.
    Moving providers then means editing this one file rather than chasing every
    place the link was shared.

    Belt and braces: a meta refresh, and a real link for anyone whose browser
    or reader ignores it. No JavaScript — a redirect that needs a script to work
    is a redirect that fails silently in exactly the readers most likely to
    block one. #}
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ subscribe_url }}">
<style>
  body {
    margin: 0; background: #ffffff; color: #16191d;
    font: 15px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 34rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.15rem; text-align: center; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  p { color: #545e69; margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }
  a.go {
    display: inline-block; background: #0b5fbe; color: #fff; text-decoration: none;
    padding: .7rem 1.3rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 700;
  }
  a.back { color: #0b5fbe; font-size: .85rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <h1>{{ brand.PUBLICATION }}</h1>
  <p>{{ brand.TAGLINE }} One email a {{ brand.CADENCE_NOUN }}, free.</p>
  <p><a class="go" href="{{ subscribe_url }}">Continue to the signup form</a></p>
  <p><a class="back" href="./">← back to the current issue</a></p>
</div>
</body>
</html>
